Musk=E2=80=99s denial has been met with skepticism given his close ties wit=
h the administration. It is impossible to disentangle him and SpaceX from t=
he Trump administration. He has realigned himself with the White House in r=
ecent months, patching up his explosive feud with the president from a year=
 ago and appearing with Trump at major events. Musk has been appointed to a=
 Pentagon commission on the future of war and has given hundreds of million=
s of dollars to conservative Republican candidates.

Musk has also personally ordered the restriction of Starlink service in Ukr=
aine before. In 2022, SpaceX cut off Starlink =E2=80=93 not StarShield =E2=
=80=93 service during a Ukrainian counteroffensive in the regions of Kherso=
n and Donetsk. He refused Ukraine=E2=80=99s request to extend connectivity =
to Crimea the same year.

One tech tycoon=E2=80=99s political leanings are determining the tides of w=
ar between two sovereign nations. Musk=E2=80=99s alliance with the White Ho=
use implicates him in the pressure campaign against Ukraine to end the war =
with Russia, likely via surrender.

