Be more human: how to resist the creep of AI


=E2=80=98We decide that we want to be more human.=E2=80=99 Photograph: Marc=
ela Barsse/Getty Images


My colleague Robert Booth reports from the Hacking Big Tech conference, a G=
uardian conference in Paris:

As the Paris Streets erupted with protest and violence on Saturday, a paral=
lel radicalism was on display at the Hacking Big Tech conference organised =
by the French media organisation Mediapart in conjunction with the Guardian=
. Amid the contributions from experts in military AI and how to fight again=
st datacentres, a theme emerged about how people might respond to the tech =
wave: be more human.

The writer Naomi Klein told the audience that the technology companies inte=
nd AI to be used as an =E2=80=9Ceverything app and also as a truth machine=
=E2=80=9D. This, she said, was =E2=80=9Cvery clearly a fascist idea, to cen=
tralise knowledge, to standardise what intelligence is=E2=80=9D.

At a rare tech conference not addressed by representatives of tech companie=
s, Klein painted a bleak AI-driven future in which there is =E2=80=9Cgoing =
to be more resource scarcity, there=E2=80=99s going to be more people who h=
ave no role in the economy and need to be contained and surveilled=E2=80=9D=
.

A response was available, she said: =E2=80=9CWe decide that we want to be m=
ore human.=E2=80=9D

Humour was another answer. German Salazar, a Chilean activist campaigning t=
o save water in his native country in the face of a wave of AI datacentres,=
 showed how his community had set up a human chatbot to encourage people to=
 prompt less and save water. The idea was simple: a team, ranging from chil=
dren to town elders, offered human responses to chatbot queries from anywhe=
re in the world for a day. If you want an image of a dog doing yoga, one of=
 them will paint it for you. Want to know what love is? A human will tell y=
ou it is =E2=80=9Cthe wish of someone else to be happy=E2=80=9D.

There were 2,300 requests for images, 135 for dating advice and one for the=
 meaning of life.

